   ("Sub-atomic particles", ["<b>Protons</b> — positive, in the nucleus; their number defines the element (atomic number).", "<b>Neutrons</b> — neutral, in the nucleus; their number adds mass without changing the element.", "<b>Electrons</b> — negative, arranged in shells outside the nucleus; in a neutral atom the number of electrons equals the number of protons."]),
   ("Key definitions", ["Atomic number (Z) = number of protons; mass number (A) = protons + neutrons. Isotopes are atoms of the same element with the same number of protons but different numbers of neutrons (e.g. Cl-35 and Cl-37). Electron configuration shows the arrangement of electrons in shells (e.g. sodium 2,8,1), which explains the chemical behaviour of the element."]),
