   ("Simple tenses", ["<b>Present</b> — habits and general truths (She <i>writes</i> every day).", "<b>Past</b> — completed actions (We <i>visited</i> Lagos last week).", "<b>Future</b> — actions that will happen (They <i>will travel</i> tomorrow)."]),
   ("Continuous and perfect forms", ["<b>Present continuous</b> — action in progress (He <i>is reading</i> now). <b>Past continuous</b> — was/were + -ing (We <i>were sleeping</i> when it rained). <b>Present perfect</b> — have/has + past participle, for actions with present relevance (She <i>has finished</i> her assignment). <b>Past perfect</b> — had + past participle (The bus <i>had left</i> before we arrived). <b>Future perfect</b> — will have + past participle (By June, I <i>will have completed</i> SS1)."]),
